    section(38,'Limitations','Annotation completeness governs normal labels. Board-group splitting can expose distribution shift. Tight crops lose trace context; whole-board windows can miss tiny defects. A single seed does not estimate variance. Scores are uncalibrated and optical inspection does not establish electrical continuity.')
